# package.json's "files": ["build/*"] is what actually controls what gets published — this file
# is a defense-in-depth backstop, not the primary mechanism. Written as an allow-list (exclude
# everything, carve out build/) rather than naming individual source directories by name: the
# previous version excluded `public/ routes/ scripts/ src/ views/`, which after the TypeScript/
# React migration (specs/001-modernize-ts-react) would have let `server/`, `client/`, `tests/`,
# `tools/`, `dist/`, and `baseline/` all leak into the published package.
*
!build/**
